uce that:\n     \\[\n     A_1A_2 + A_1A_{11} = 20 - (A_1A_3 + A_1A_4 + \\ldots + A_1A_{10})\n     \\]\n   - Since each \\( A_iA_{i+1} = \\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{13} \\), the sum of the lengths of the remaining sides is:\n     \\[\n     A_1A_3 + A_1A_4 + \\ldots + A_1A_{10} = 8 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{13} = \\frac{8\\sqrt{26}}{13}\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, we have:\n     \\[\n     A_1A_2 + A_1A_{11} = 20 - \\frac{8\\sqrt{26}}{13} = \\frac{260 - 8\\sqrt{26}}{13}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n   - The expression \\( A_1A_2 + A_1A_{11} \\) is in the form \\( \\frac{m\\sqrt{n} - p}{q} \\) with \\( m = 260 \\), \\( n = 26 \\), \\( p = 8 \\), and \\( q = 13 \\).\n   - Therefore, \\( m + n + p + q = 260 + 26 + 8 + 13 = 307 \\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{307}\\).",
